<title>BRAZIL: POLL - Consensus survey of Brazilian indicators.</title>
<headline>POLL - Consensus survey of Brazilian indicators.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are consensus forecasts from a survey of economic indicators taken from eight Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro brokerages and research firms. Also included are current market rates for dollar and interest rate futures over the next three months.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>*****Brazil Indicators - July Consensus Forecast*****</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>INDICATOR	  PERIOD   AVG FORECAST  MEDIAN    PRVS MONTH</p>
<p>CPI (Fipe)	  July    0.54  pct    0.40  pct  1.42  pct</p>
<p>PPI (IPA-M/FGV)   July    0.40  pct    0.40  pct  0.32  pct</p>
<p>Inflation (IGP-M) July    0.32  pct    0.48  pct  0.74  pct</p>
<p>Ind Act (IBGE)    June    6.17  pct    6.06  pct  N.A.</p>
<p>Trade Balance     July    -$570  million   -$553 million  -$466  million</p>
<p>Exports	     July    $5.030 bln   $5.18 bln  $4.843 bln</p>
<p>Imports	     July    $5.600 bln   $5.70 bln  $5.309 bln</p>
<p>				   ******</p>
<p>		Brazilian Financial Indicators</p>
<p>	   Futures market rates at July 30 close</p>
<p>			 August	  September     October</p>
<p>Real/Dollar	   1.0914	  1.0993	  1.1075</p>
<p>Monthly Int Rates   1.620 pct     1.630  pct    1.660 pct</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTES: Price indicators reflect monthly variation.</p>
<p>Industrial activity reflects annual variation.</p>
<p>((-- John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248-5414))</p>
